{
  "title": "Pangea™ PeriPRO™ Distal Femur Plate",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/implants/423203/pangea-tm--peripro-tm--distal-femur-plate",
  "subtitle": "Distal Femur Fractures Updated: Jun 9 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Related Implants",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "The Pangea™ series contains 3 PeriPro femur plates",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**Proximal Femur**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Distal Femur (this topic)**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "**Interprosthetic Femur**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Pangea Design",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Variable Angle Locking Technology**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Pangea’s variable angle locking technology uses a CoCr locking screw, which is harder than the Ti6Al4V ELI plate, allowing for the screwhead’s threads to form a definitive locking position in the plate’s locking hole by engaging the softer, Ti6Al4V ELI material.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "This technology allows the user to aim and lock the screw into the plate within a true 30° cone of the predetermined hole trajectory. The variable angle drill guide provided with the system offers guidance with respect to the limit of the 30° cone. The locking mechanism remains functional for up to three attempts at locking screw insertion.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Tapered End**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed for atraumatic submuscular insertion",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Cable Plug Compatible Holes**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Cable plugs accepted in any round screw hole and may be used in conjunction with a 2.0mm vitallium cable",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Staggered Screw Pattern**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Staggered screw hole trajectories in the diaphysis are designed to accommodate screw placement in the anterior and posterior cortex around an intramedullary nail or a prosthesis.",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423203/images/40a19eec-52fc-4b5e-be5d-10aa8c78831f_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.58.55_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Waisted Scalloped Shape**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "**Oblong Hole**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "To aid in plate placement and serve as an attachment site for targeter",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "**Metaphyseal Screw Cluster**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "Designed to provide anatomic fixation through size adapted options",
              "table": null,
              "images": [
                {
                  "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/423203/images/20bc3929-3f6c-4153-897e-e0372fd4d383_screenshot_2025-01-14_at_3.58.59_pm.jpg",
                  "caption": ""
                }
              ],
              "importance": "-1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Placement",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radius of Curvature and distal screw cluster plate width changes for longest plate length to fascilitate fit",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
